# AWS drift report (Cursor rule)

For Cursor versions without Agent Skills. Newer Cursor versions can load `skills/aws-drift-report/SKILL.md`
directly from `~/.cursor/skills/aws-drift-report/`; this rule says the same thing in short form.

Run the `aws-drift-report` CLI (`pip install aws-drift-report`, or `python3 <repo>/skills/aws-drift-report/scripts/drift_report.py`):

- Terraform/OpenTofu directory: `aws-drift-report terraform --dir <dir> --format md`
  (needs `.terraform/`; ask before running `tofu init`). Credentials from `AWS_PROFILE`.
- Saved plan JSON: `aws-drift-report terraform --plan-json plan.json`
- CloudFormation: `aws-drift-report cloudformation --profile <p> --region <r> [--stack NAME ...]`
- Not in IaC (resources no state file or stack lists): `aws-drift-report unmanaged --profile <p> --region <r>
  --state s3://<bucket>/<prefix>/` (`--state` may repeat: a `.tfstate`, an S3 key or prefix, or an initialised
  directory; `--all-regions` for every region). Ask where the state lives; never print state contents.
- Other formats: `--format html|csv|json -o <file>`; `--fail-on-drift` exits 2 for CI.

Rules: read-only. Never run `apply`, `import`, `state` or `refresh` commands, never edit state files, never
change AWS resources. CloudFormation `DetectStackDrift` is allowed; the not-in-IaC scan only lists and describes. Ask for the AWS profile and region if
unclear. Summarise counts by severity first, then explain high rows (security groups, IAM, public access,
encryption, KMS) and suggest a fix: revert in AWS or update the code. Keep the report's footer line as is.
